box-model-sketch-0.bodyMarkdown:
Links are inline by default. `inline-block` keeps them in the inline flow while allowing box-model spacing to behave more like a box.

```css
nav a {
  display: inline-block;
}
```

**Line by line:** `nav a` selects the existing navigation links. `display: inline-block` keeps them next to one another while allowing padding and margins to form predictable clickable boxes.

box-model-sketch-1.bodyMarkdown:
The inherited Projects page contains a table. On a narrow screen, wide table content should scroll instead of forcing the whole page wider.

```css
table {
  display: block;
  overflow-x: auto;
}
```

**Line by line:** `table` selects the existing table. `display: block` lets it participate as a block container here. `overflow-x: auto` adds horizontal scrolling only when the table needs it.

box-model-sketch-2.bodyMarkdown:
The inherited Contact form already has labels. A block label gives each field a clear line start.

```css
form label {
  display: block;
}
```

**Line by line:** `form label` selects labels only inside the existing form. `display: block` makes each label begin on a new line without changing the form's semantic HTML.
